            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial revascularization in a sickle-cell trait patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>603-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 56-year-old man with confirmed sickle-cell trait AS underwent successful triple-vessel myocardial revascularization with internal mammary artery and vein conduits. Variations in routine technique included limitation in hypothermia (32 degrees C), avoidance of intraoperative autologous salvage, hypoxia, severe anemia (&lt; 25% hematocrit), acidosis and postoperative reinfusion of mediastinal drainage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
